-- title:
--   Hopf-flat p-torsion subgroups lie in the finite part
-- statement:
--   Fix natural numbers $N_0$ and $p$ with $p$ prime and $p \nmid N_0$, and a valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbf{Q}}$ lying over $p$, in the sense that $p$ is a non-unit of $A$. Let $\Lambda$ be level data for $(N_0,p,A)$ satisfying the conjunction of conditions `IsJacobian` (abelian-scheme property, commutativity of the relative group law, additivity and Galois-equivariance of the point parametrisations, compatibility of reduction modulo the place, and realisation of the Hecke algebra by endomorphisms over the base), let $O$ be a Néron object `JZeroNeronObjectAtP` for these data, and let $F$ be a Néron extension of $O$ over the strictly henselian ring attached to $A$. Assume the two monodromy inclusions for $O$: for $m$ coprime to $p$, every $\sigma$ in the inertia subgroup of $A$ over $\mathbf{Q}$ (the image in $\mathrm{Aut}(\overline{\mathbf{Q}}/\mathbf{Q})$ of the inertia subgroup inside the decomposition subgroup) and every $m$-torsion $x$ of $\mathrm{Pic}^0$ of the level-$N_0p$ modular function field satisfy $\sigma\cdot x-x\in O.\mathrm{toricPts}\,m$; and for every $m>0$ the same differences lie in $O.\mathrm{finPts}\,m$, the subgroup generated by $m$-torsion points whose $O$-point extends to a point over $A$. Assume $p\neq 2$. Let $V$ be a subgroup of the $p$-torsion, and let $H$ be a commutative ring which is a finite flat cocommutative Hopf algebra over the subring of $\mathbf{Q}$ of rationals with denominator coprime to $p$, together with a bijection $e$ from the convolution monoid of algebra maps $H\to\overline{\mathbf{Q}}$ onto $V$ carrying products to sums and such that, whenever $g=\sigma\circ f$ pointwise on $H$ for a field automorphism $\sigma$ of $\overline{\mathbf{Q}}$ over $\mathbf{Q}$, one has $e(g)=\sigma\cdot e(f)$ in the Picard group. Then $V$ is contained in $F.\mathrm{finPts}\,p$, the subgroup generated by the $p$-torsion points satisfying the extension predicate $F.\mathrm{ExtN}$.
--
--   This is the Raynaud prolongation step at $p\neq2$: a subgroup of $J_0(N_0p)[p]$ presented as the points of a finite flat commutative, cocommutative group scheme over $\mathbf{Z}_{(p)}$ prolongs into the finite part of the Néron model over the inertia-invariant valuation ring, in the hypothesis-carrying form in which the two monodromy inclusions for the Néron object are assumed. It feeds the construction of ordinary level-$p$ data via [`ModularCurve.JZeroNeronObjectAtP.exists_jZeroNeronAtPDataOrdV22_of_children_of_neronExtension`](thm.html#ModularCurve.JZeroNeronObjectAtP.exists_jZeroNeronAtPDataOrdV22_of_children_of_neronExtension).
